]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"202ea3cb5665914924afbb78be43747c2360dd2383ff0f7b0436bff4bac2b167","event_uuid":"cb1447b7-eab2-456c-b327-2be870a0664e","position":{"commit_sha":"72c6b13c4ae9ad458b0d6f3adb59df2e9fc84323","position":"1787692214877351001-cb1447b7-eab2-456c-b327-2be870a0664e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787677898259610001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dfe3631b-c4ba-406c-ad4f-8a0e77511e8f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d109-30bb-c40d-4c13"},{"link_uuid":"64c68f60-98c6-4e1e-a3b1-42e7301f7112","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e33b-6837-6693-49f7"},{"link_uuid":"a95dc83f-3748-4f18-b21a-df251deed150","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e91a-d447-0a0f-47e4"}],"description":"The mcp service in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` does not set `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL`.\nOn a fresh deploy the container crash-loops before serving: `AuthSettings` (pydantic) raises a\nValidationError because `issuer_url` is empty (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py` ~L609,\n`AuthSettings(issuer_url=mcp_cfg.auth_issuer_url, ...)`), and `/health` never comes up.\n\n## Root cause (surfaced by jackal live deploy)\nThe compose mcp `environment:` block sets `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL` (compose ~L347)\nbut omits the sibling `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL`. `fetch-secrets.sh` does not inject it either,\nso the container boots with an empty issuer URL and fails auth-settings construction.\n\n## Live impact\nOn the prod box the endpoint only came up after a temporary `.env` hotfix appending\n`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL=https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`. Autodeploy rsync from main\nwill drop that hotfix and can re-crash the mcp container on the next blue-green tick.\n\n## Fix\nAdd to the mcp `environment:` block, mirroring how RESOURCE_SERVER_URL is set:\n`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL: \"${REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL:-https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp}\"`\n\n## RED-first oracle\nA compose-assertion test that parses docker-compose.yml and asserts the mcp service environment\ndefines a non-empty `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL` (fails today, passes after the fix). Note:\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py` always sets `auth_issuer_url` explicitly, so unit\ntests never caught the compose omission — the gap is deploy config, not the auth code.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] RED compose-assertion test proves the mcp service env omits a non-empty issuer URL, then passes after the fix.\n- [x] docker-compose.yml mcp environment sets REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL (default to the prod /mcp URL, overridable).\n- [x] [operator-attested] Lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1).\n  provenance: environment=Gerrit main gate (rebar.solutions.navateam.com) + GitHub Actions Verified Gate; principal=rebar review bot + rebar CI bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — change 2222 (patchset 2, commit 799ba486196f) merged to main with LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"Add REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL to the mcp service environment (mirrors RESOURCE_SERVER_URL) so AuthSettings constructs on a fresh deploy."},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Mirror the same REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL env in the blue-green docker run so autodeploy stays in parity with compose (enforced by test_docker_run_matches_compose_mcp_service)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py","reason":"RED-first compose-assertion: the mcp service env must define a non-empty REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e33b-6837-6693-49f7"],["relates_to","e91a-d447-0a0f-47e4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5d06f46c-b6f2-4231-9ce4-51776910939b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ed3b-0c32-a043-4c5d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"mcp compose service omits REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL -> AuthSettings crash-loop on fresh deploy","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["031aba1c-687f-4250-8680-0bee488c58d8","718af1bc-ae9c-410e-8fc4-bdae439f654c","58f50399-a8d2-47eb-989d-348c1f091833","f7c4e3b4-c90d-45a2-bed8-7a52fdb06cf6","64c68f60-98c6-4e1e-a3b1-42e7301f7112","48cf6f5c-d2ef-4ae8-b8ec-eb5c63bd9867","a95dc83f-3748-4f18-b21a-df251deed150","01c694d1-40dc-48de-bf27-0fb993884128","fd3dacef-4e64-4cc5-9704-9fbaa6c096b9","bc28e3ed-2857-467f-accc-c73c70e62350","05eb52be-2e82-48b5-82a4-b2c84470218d","5d06f46c-b6f2-4231-9ce4-51776910939b","cb1447b7-eab2-456c-b327-2be870a0664e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787713811061851001,"uuid":"c94fb01f-7907-4eb1-99c9-e77e186f5c23"}